Scope
-----
This branch contains the follow-up root fix for the still-reproducible Agent
2-way voice and incoming Agent CallKit silence/routing defects. It is isolated
from the concurrent Agent Chat work. Merge it into the Agent Chat integration
branch, keep both sets of changes, then perform one combined TestFlight build
only after the owner explicitly approves it.

Confirmed root causes
---------------------
1. CallKit cold/background answer fulfilled CXAnswerCallAction before the app
   prepared AVAudioSession as playAndRecord + voiceChat. CallKit therefore
   activated whichever stale/default category and route existed. Foregrounding
   the app or toggling speaker later rebuilt/re-routed the graph, explaining the
   delayed recovery.
2. A cold in-app 2-way voice start unconditionally called live.stop() before the
   first live.start(). That queued AVAudioSession.setActive(false) directly in
   front of the initial configure/start path. Re-entering the page worked because
   the lifecycle timing was different on the second attempt.
3. The app treated websocket/model “speaking” state and AVAudioEngine.isRunning
   as proof of audible playback. A VoiceProcessingIO renderer can claim running
   while no player samples advance, leaving visible speaking text with silence.
4. Route repair was one-directional: it corrected receiver -> speaker only.
   Speaker OFF did not repair speaker -> receiver. Other in-process audio users
   can also leave defaultToSpeaker on the shared AVAudioSession, making .none a
   no-op unless the stale option is removed.
5. The previous TestFlight diagnostics only reported terminal connection failure
   or a one-time route check. They could not distinguish “PCM received, UI says
   speaking, render clock stalled,” so the actual device-only failure was hidden.

Implemented changes
-------------------
- Prepares the CallKit AVAudioSession category/mode before action.fulfill(), but
  leaves activation exclusively to CallKit.
- Fails the CallKit answer if audio preflight fails and does not mark the backend
  call answered in that case.
- Pre-activates standalone in-app audio once and skips live.stop() on the first
  cold start; retry teardown remains intact.
- Removes defaultToSpeaker from this live voice owner and explicitly enforces
  both speaker and receiver routes, with bounded actual-route verification.
- Avoids unnecessary category resets while CallKit audio is active; resets only
  if category/mode/defaultToSpeaker is stale.
- Primes the cold playback graph after real model PCM is queued.
- Verifies that the player render sample clock advances. If it stalls, performs
  one graph restart, re-enforces the requested route, and verifies recovery.
- Adds release-safe timing/category/route/input/PCM/render traces containing no
  transcript, token, URL, credential, or user content. Unrecovered Agent-call
  failures attach a compact trace tail to the server call note.
- Adds regression contract assertions for answer ordering, first-start teardown,
  two-way route enforcement, and render-stall detection/recovery.

