Physical-device boundary
------------------------
The registered physical iPhone was offline during verification:

  iPhone, iOS 26.5.2, UDID 00008150-00097C390A40401C — OFFLINE

A simulator cannot prove PushKit delivery, genuine CallKit activation, receiver
acoustics, loudspeaker acoustics, or proximity behavior. These checks remain
mandatory on a signed real-device/TestFlight build.

Integration instructions
------------------------
1. Preserve/commit the Agent Chat session's own work.
2. Merge branch codex/ios-voice-audio-root-fix-v2. Resolve conflicts by retaining
   both Chat changes and every audio invariant below.
3. Run the combined Agent Chat suite plus:

     npm test -- --run src/agent/lib/__tests__/native-voice-upload-contract.test.ts

4. Build and launch on the dedicated iPhone 17 Pro simulator. Verify first-entry
   2-way voice starts without leaving/re-entering and inspect Audio trace events.
5. Before TestFlight, review these invariants:
   - prepareCallKitAudioSession occurs before CXAnswerCallAction.fulfill;
   - CallKit-owned code never calls setActive(true);
   - cold first start does not call live.stop();
   - no defaultToSpeaker in Gemini live audio ownership;
   - speaker and receiver routes are both enforced and verified;
   - speaking UI is not accepted without advancing rendered samples.
6. Ask the owner before any archive/upload/distribution.

Hard real-iPhone acceptance checklist
-------------------------------------
[ ] Fresh app launch -> Agent 2-way voice -> first attempt is immediately audible.
[ ] User microphone input works on that same first attempt.
[ ] Incoming Agent call answered in foreground -> immediate two-way audio.
[ ] Incoming Agent call answered in background -> immediate two-way audio.
[ ] Incoming Agent call answered from lock screen -> immediate two-way audio.
[ ] Speaker ON -> loud built-in speaker; reported route matches.
[ ] Speaker OFF -> quiet built-in receiver/earpiece; reported route matches.
[ ] Receiver proximity blanks/restores screen near/far from ear.
[ ] Repeated speaker ON/OFF does not start audio accidentally; audio was already live.
[ ] CallKit mute/unmute controls the actual microphone.
[ ] Deactivate/reactivate or interruption resumes without foregrounding/toggling.
[ ] Network reconnect does not leave a silent LIVE timer.
[ ] End/reset leaves no timer, graph, proximity state, or call UI behind.

TestFlight gate
---------------
DO NOT archive, upload, submit, or distribute automatically. After the combined
branch passes simulator tests, compile, invariant review, and any available
signed-device checks, ask exactly:

  “Agent Chat + Agent voice fixes একসাথে hard-verified। এখন কি TestFlight
   archive/upload শুরু করব?”

Proceed only after an explicit YES. Produce one combined TestFlight build from
the Agent Chat integration branch, not a separate build from this handoff branch.
